ist":-0.03791634026820166,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":0.022840892960561895,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":11.4,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.486807888545134,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.03494902733826908,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":28.3,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.028538995091902032,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":42.8,"_gate_pool_share":-0.07329691229632518,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":10.7,"_gate_rev_durability":0.5791703190225568,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.1835189186669719,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.009517355130283924,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":40.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.021200835588339934,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":34.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.029608671365329187,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":13.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012131930382123906,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":79.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.22754,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Astrana Health, Inc., a healthcare management company, provides medical care services in the United States. The company operates through three segments: Care Partners, Care Delivery, and Care Enablement. The company offers care coordination services to patients, families, primary care physicians, specialists, acute care hospitals, alternative sites of inpatient care, physician groups, and health plans. Its physician network includes primary care physicians, specialist physicians and extenders, and hospitalists. The company serves patients primarily covered by private or public insurance, such as Medicare, Medicaid, and health maintenance organization; and non-insured patients. The company was formerly known as Apollo Medical Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to Astrana Health, Inc. in February 2024. Astrana Health, Inc. was founded in 1992 and is headquartered in Alhambra, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brandon K. Sim M.S. | President & CEO | Age 31 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 58%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $35K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Astrana Health Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.6B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +41% over the past three years and +58% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 19% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $104M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.10\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 23% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (39% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 41% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 23% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Astrana Health (ASTH) Earnings Beat Puts Valuation Back In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-asth/astrana-health/news/astrana-health-asth-earnings-beat-puts-valuation-back-in-foc","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572748.78,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.751,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Astrana Health (ASTH) Stock May Be Fully Priced On Record Q3 Results","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-asth/astrana-health/news/astrana-health-asth-stock-may-be-fully-priced-on-record-q3-r","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794148048.762,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Astrana signals at least mid-teens adjusted EBITDA growth into 2027 while forecasting 10%-15% Medicaid membership decline (NASDAQ:ASTH)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668512-astrana-signals-at-least-mid-teens-adjusted-ebitda-growth-into-2027-while-forecasting-10","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793997458.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Astrana Health (NASDAQ:ASTH) Stock Price Expected to Rise, Needham & Company LLC Analyst Says","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/astrana-health-nasdaqasth-stock-price-expected-to-rise-needham-company-llc-analyst-says.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793970783.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Astrana Health (ASTH) Following Results T